From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:03:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: give CAMSS the TOP GDSC it votes
 for

CAMSS on msm8998 declares only the two VFE GDSCs, so nothing ever powers
CAMSS_TOP_GDSC on its behalf. Every CSIPHY clock list starts with
"top_ahb" -- CAMSS_TOP_AHB_CLK, which lives under that GDSC -- and
csiphy_set_power() reaches it through pm_runtime_resume_and_get() on the
camss device alone. With the domain unattached the vote never happens:

  camss_top_ahb_clk status stuck at 'off'
   camss_enable_clocks+0x4c/0xdc [qcom_camss]
   csiphy_set_power+0x238/0x324 [qcom_camss]
   video_prepare_streaming+0x1c/0x58 [qcom_camss]
  qcom-camss ca00020.camss: clock enable failed: -16
  qcom-camss ca00020.camss: Failed to power up pipeline: -16

It went unnoticed because the sensor drivers used to hold themselves
runtime-active from probe to unbind, which pinned CAMSS_TOP for the life
of every boot. Letting them idle -- worth 244 mW on taimen -- removed the
accidental vote and left the pipeline unable to raise it.

This is what the hardware's own vendor tree does. In msm8998-camera.dtsi
every camera block takes a CAMSS_TOP vote of its own:
qcom,csiphy@ca34000, all four CSIDs, both VFEs and qcom,cci@ca0c000 each
carry "gdscr-supply = <&gdsc_camss_top>", and the CSIPHY node lists
clk_mmss_camss_top_ahb_clk among its clocks. Mainline describes the whole
block as one device, so the single-node form of that is the block GDSC on
the camss node -- exactly as sdm845 already does with TITAN_TOP_GDSC.

camss_configure_pd() needs no change: it treats a power-domain count
greater than the number of VFEs flagged has_pd as the block domain, takes
it by the last index and links it DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME | DL_FLAG_RPM_ACTIVE.
Last position in the list is therefore load-bearing.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8998-camss.yaml          | 1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi                          | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8998-camss.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8998-camss.yaml
index bad54b7fb9ec..08f8404694d4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8998-camss.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8998-camss.yaml
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@ properties:
     items:
       - description: VFE0 GDSC - Video Front End, Global Distributed Switch Controller.
       - description: VFE1 GDSC - Video Front End, Global Distributed Switch Controller.
+      - description: CAMSS TOP GDSC - CAMSS Top Block, Global Distributed Switch Controller.
 
   ports:
     $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/properties/ports
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index 7a86b176ac1c..bf870a0969ee 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -4468,7 +4468,8 @@ camss: camss@ca00000 {
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0xc03>;
 
 			power-domains = <&mmcc CAMSS_VFE0_GDSC>,
-					<&mmcc CAMSS_VFE1_GDSC>;
+					<&mmcc CAMSS_VFE1_GDSC>,
+					<&mmcc CAMSS_TOP_GDSC>;
 
 			status = "disabled";
 
